  "claim": "The animated film Gwen Stefani's song, \"Shine\", is featured in was released in 2014. The star of Into the Dalek also played the role of Mr Curry in the sequel of that animated film in 2017.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Peter Capaldi. Sentence: Peter Dougan Capaldi (born 14 April 1958) is a Scottish actor, writer and director, best known for playing the twelfth incarnation of the Doctor in \"Doctor Who\" and as spin doctor Malcolm Tucker in \"The Thick of It\", for which he has received four British Academy Television Award nominations, winning Best Male Comedy Performance in 2010.\nPage: Peter Capaldi. Sentence: He further took on the role of Paddington Bear's neighbour Mr. Curry in the family comedy film \"Paddington\"; he is set to reprise the role in \"Paddington 2\".\nPage: Paddington 2. Sentence: Paddington 2 is an upcoming British-French family-comedy film directed by Paul King, co written by King and Simon Farnaby, and produced by David Heyman.\nPage: Paddington 2. Sentence: The film is set to release on 10 November 2017.\nPage: Into the Dalek. Sentence: Starring Peter Capaldi and Jenna Coleman the episode also introduces Samuel Anderson as Danny Pink.\nPage: Shine (Gwen Stefani song). Sentence: It is a reggae pop and ska song that is featured in the 2014 animated film \"Paddington.\"",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Peter Capaldi. Sentence: Peter Dougan Capaldi (born 14 April 1958) is a Scottish actor, writer and director, best known for playing the twelfth incarnation of the Doctor in \"Doctor Who\" and as spin doctor Malcolm Tucker in \"The Thick of It\", for which he has received four British Academy Television Award nominations, winning Best Male Comedy Performance in 2010.\nPage: Peter Capaldi. Sentence: He further took on the role of Paddington Bear's neighbour Mr. Curry in the family comedy film \"Paddington\"; he is set to reprise the role in \"Paddington 2\".\nPage: Paddington 2. Sentence: Paddington 2 is an upcoming British-French family-comedy film directed by Paul King, co written by King and Simon Farnaby, and produced by David Heyman.\nPage: Paddington 2. Sentence: The film is set to release on 10 November 2017.\nPage: Into the Dalek. Sentence: Starring Peter Capaldi and Jenna Coleman the episode also introduces Samuel Anderson as Danny Pink.\nPage: Shine (Gwen Stefani song). Sentence: It is a reggae pop and ska song that is featured in the 2014 animated film \"Paddington.\"",
